API-08: make a bad EN_addrule string leave existing rules alone

On an error EN_addrule deleted rule number Nrules, but Nrules only
grows once a valid RULE clause has been read. A bad first clause or a
bad RULE line therefore deleted the previous rule, or took Nrules to -1
when there was none. A leading DISABLED clause was also accepted and
disabled the previous rule. EN_addrule now returns 221 unless the first
clause is RULE, and deletes a rule only if this call added one. It uses
the rule count that the CRASH-17 fix records on entry.

Requires: CRASH-17

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb, after CRASH-17:
    git apply API-08_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index d9b0835..00e9ae1 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -5658,6 +5658,13 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_addrule(EN_Project p, char *rule)
         // Process the line to build up the rule's contents
         if (parser->Ntokens > 0 && *parser->Tok[0] != ';')
         {
+            // The first clause must start the new rule
+            if (net->Nrules == nrules && !match(parser->Tok[0], w_RULE))
+            {
+                rules->Errcode = 221;
+                break;
+            }
+
             // Only one rule can be added at a time
             if (net->Nrules > nrules && match(parser->Tok[0], w_RULE))
             {
@@ -5674,7 +5681,7 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_addrule(EN_Project p, char *rule)
     }
 
     // Delete new rule entry if there was an error
-    if (rules->Errcode) deleterule(p, net->Nrules);
+    if (rules->Errcode && net->Nrules > nrules) deleterule(p, net->Nrules);
 
     // Re-assign error code 201 (syntax error) to 250 (invalid format)
     if (rules->Errcode == 201) rules->Errcode = 250;
